# Shell scripts must stay LF so the committed gate runner executes on any OS.
*.sh text eol=lf
# EVERY file the defect pass mutates must stay LF in the WORKING TREE, because
# its mutations are multi-line perl patterns using \n. Under core.autocrlf=true a
# `git checkout` rewrites a checked-out file to CRLF, and \n then matches nothing
# -- which silently broke seven defect rows on 2026-09-14. They did not error;
# they reported GATE: PASS while planting nothing. The blobs were LF throughout;
# only the working copy was converted, by the recovery step itself.
*.js   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
# Binary assets -- never apply text/EOL conversion.
*.png binary
# Fixtures are DATA THE GATES PARSE, and they fall through the rule above because
# it lists source extensions. A real 100-row response landed in tests/fixtures/ on
# 2026-09-15 and git immediately warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time
# Git touches it" -- the same trap as the seven dead defect rows, aimed this time
# at a file the harness reads. Nothing was broken when it was spotted (working copy
# and blob were both LF); the trap springs on the next checkout. A guard that
# covers the files you happened to think of is not a guard.
*.json text eol=lf
